<!-- People › Skills & training (design-people §10, §1.2; impl-people P18): the skills matrix (Development/SkillsMatrix, the default,
    a .qvue matrix with its terminal twin SkillsMatrixTui out of the menu), Qualifications and (P19) Training, with TrainingDetail and
    TrainingCertificate out of the menu. Every People
    user opens the area through the root, and what each sees is what Mantle's DevelopmentServices admit: the matrix to development
    and HR readers of the employer and to a manager for their reports; qualifications to the person, development, HR, a manager
    and the other staff readers, each at their level (an identity document's or work permit's number the person's and HR's alone;
    a manager and other staff readers verified ones' validity only). A self-service employee without the launcher opens the area
    by its own grant (BOSS_PPL_DEVELOPMENT), for their own qualifications and training (the sessions of their employers, their own
    places, results and certificates, and the sessions they train); the matrix is denied to them (BOSS_PPL_SKILLS). -->
<screen xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/xml-screen-3.xsd"
        default-menu-title="Skills &amp; training" default-menu-index="12" menu-image="sym_o_school" menu-image-type="icon">
    <subscreens default-item="SkillsMatrix">
        <!-- SkillsMatrix (menu index 1), Qualifications (2) and Training (3) are files under Development/, with SkillsMatrixTui,
            TrainingDetail and TrainingCertificate out of the menu -->
    </subscreens>
    <widgets>
        <subscreens-active/>
    </widgets>
</screen>
